index 00000000..980b2832
--- /dev/null
+++ b/specs/packages/skill-runtime.md
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# skill-runtime: Standalone Runtime Distribution
+
+## Intent
+
+Keep a standalone agent client on one auditable SPEX runtime and host Playbook engine.
+
+## External Behavior
+
+### skill-runtime-1
+
+When distributing the standalone runtime, the builder shall rebuild the CLI, Core and built-in content from one recorded upstream commit with a published source patch and locked dependencies.
+
+### skill-runtime-2
+
+When a local Core-owned endpoint starts, the Core shall publish its protocol, process, port and bearer in a private endpoint descriptor, withdrawing only its own descriptor on shutdown.
+
+### skill-runtime-3
+
+When session creation includes an expected workflow identity, the Core shall refuse an identity, command, package or version no longer present in the project's effective composition.
+
+### skill-runtime-4
+
+When runtime diagnostics are requested, the serving Core shall report its build source, installed packages and each placed registry's static engine import resolution without executing a workflow or exposing credentials.
+
+### skill-runtime-7
+
+When a new run is requested, the standalone client shall refuse an unverified engine resolution or a Core build differing from the distributed build before creating a session.
+
+### skill-runtime-9
+
+When native file notifications fail synchronously or asynchronously, the standalone Core shall retain file-change observation through polling without crashing or changing host permissions.
+
+### skill-runtime-11
+
+When a temporary Core's owning client finishes, the owner shall retain that Core until its other direct local API clients disconnect, without aborting their operations or removing the root lease to start another writer.
+
+## Verification
+
+### skill-runtime-5
+
+Distribution integration tests shall prepare an isolated runtime and check matching CLI/Core build provenance and freshly staged built-in content [[skill-runtime-1](#skill-runtime-1)], attach through the published endpoint [[skill-runtime-2](#skill-runtime-2)] and diagnose installed workflow imports including replaced stale engine links [[skill-runtime-4](#skill-runtime-4)].
+
+### skill-runtime-6
+
+Session integration tests shall reject a changed selected workflow before execution [[skill-runtime-3](#skill-runtime-3)].
+
+### skill-runtime-8
+
+Installation integration tests shall preserve a real user-owned dependency directory and refuse a new session when that directory supplies a different engine [[skill-runtime-7](#skill-runtime-7)].
+
+### skill-runtime-10
+
+Integration tests shall start the actual Core with unavailable native watchers, observe an external configuration change and continue project operations without creating a workflow session [[skill-runtime-9](#skill-runtime-9)].
+
+### skill-runtime-12
+
+Integration tests shall complete concurrent local client operations against the actual temporary Core without losing their connections, then confirm normal shutdown without creating a workflow session [[skill-runtime-11](#skill-runtime-11)].
